## Seat adjudication (instrument-impl, appended after scoring — no new requests)

AUTHORITATIVE SCORING SECTION: the LAST "## GT + scoring at close" block above
(ACCURACY 20/20 = 1.000 -> PASS). The earlier score blocks are the debugging
trail of three instrument defects, kept append-only per lane idiom:

- DEFECT A (matcher, fixed pre-adjudication): the first match window
  [t0-0.5s, t0+3.0s] rejected every trial — journal stamps carry 1-second
  resolution, so a shim REQUEST stamp can sit up to 1 s BEFORE the client's
  recorded t0 (the lane's anti-pattern 15 class). Fix: window [t0-1.0, t0+3.0].
- DEFECT B (matcher, fixed pre-adjudication): parse_ts computed UTC wall time
  then called naive .timestamp(), re-applying the host's -03 offset — journal
  epochs shifted +3 h, zero candidates. Fix: epoch computed from the naive
  UTC datetime directly (no local-offset re-application).
- DEFECT C (matcher, fixed pre-adjudication): 1-second stamp truncation can
  pull the NEXT trial's stamp into the previous trial's +3 s window
  (T07's stamp 10:21:27 inside T06's window [23.1, 27.1]) -> spurious
  AMBIGUOUS(2) on T06/T10 and a first adjudication of 18/18. Fix: greedy
  in-order 1:1 assignment over window-filtered candidates (trials are strictly
  sequential, >=2.5 s spacing, and the journal window contains exactly
  20 REQUEST lines / 20 rids for 20 trials — zero interleaved traffic).
  Re-adjudication: 20/20 matched, 0 excluded.

FROZEN-TABLE CALIBRATION DEFECTS EXPOSED BY THE TRIALS (recorded, table stays
as frozen — sha 9f0244bb…; fixes belong to the next instantiation):

- D1: the ds leg-1 wall_band [0.8, 4.0] and the frozen bands generally were
  never stressed (all 20 GT legs = alibaba-token-plan; hyper and opencode-go
  UNTESTED — 0 GT trials each). The ds accuracy claim covers ONE exercised
  leg; roster coverage is partial by GT, not by prediction.
- D2: the devin prompt_tokens band [326, 488] (r19 basis, 407) missed the
  second billing mode the glm trials observed (151) — bimodal billing; see
  the glm receipt. No ds trial hit devin, so this did not affect ds scoring.
- D3: the error-path design could not force a ds error (temperature body is
  servable on leg-1; content filter did not trigger) — ds error_path_trials=0
  as frozen; error_tells stays validated by r19 receipts + mock-smoke only.

